3.1 Supervised Learning
Definition

Supervised Learning is a type of Machine Learning in which the model learns from labelled data, where the correct output is already known.

Example
Input	Output
Study 2 hours	Fail
Study 5 hours	Pass
Study 8 hours	Pass

The model learns the relationship between input and output.

Main Types
Classification
Regression
Examples
Spam detection
Student result prediction
House price prediction
Key Point

Supervised Learning = Labelled Data

3.2 Unsupervised Learning
Definition

Unsupervised Learning is a type of Machine Learning in which the model learns from unlabelled data and discovers hidden patterns or groups by itself.

There is no predefined correct output.

Example

A company has customer data:

Customer 1
Customer 2
Customer 3
Customer 4
...

The ML algorithm can automatically group similar customers.

Main Task

Clustering

Example
Customers
    ↓
ML Algorithm
    ↓
Group 1 | Group 2 | Group 3
Key Point

Unsupervised Learning = Unlabelled Data

3.3 Reinforcement Learning
Definition

Reinforcement Learning is a type of Machine Learning in which an agent learns by interacting with an environment and receiving rewards or penalties for its actions.

Basic Concept
Agent
  ↓
Takes Action
  ↓
Environment
  ↓
Reward / Penalty
  ↓
Learns
Example

A computer learns to play a game.

Good move → Reward
Bad move → Penalty

The system gradually learns which actions produce better results.

Key Point

Reinforcement Learning = Reward + Penalty

