5. Machine Learning Workflow
Definition

Machine Learning Workflow is a sequence of steps followed to collect data, prepare it, train a model, test it and use it for prediction.

Complete Workflow
Problem Definition
       ↓
Data Collection
       ↓
Data Preprocessing
       ↓
Feature Selection
       ↓
Train-Test Split
       ↓
Model Selection
       ↓
Model Training
       ↓
Model Testing / Evaluation
       ↓
Prediction
Step 1: Problem Definition
Definition

Problem Definition is the process of clearly identifying the problem that the ML model needs to solve.

Example:

Predict whether a student will pass or fail.

Step 2: Data Collection
Definition

Data Collection is the process of gathering relevant data required to solve the ML problem.

Data can come from:

Databases
CSV files
Websites
Surveys
Sensors
Applications
Step 3: Data Preprocessing
Definition

Data Preprocessing is the process of cleaning and preparing raw data before giving it to a Machine Learning model.

It may include:

Handling missing values
Removing duplicates
Correcting errors
Data transformation
Feature selection
Step 4: Feature Selection
Definition

Feature Selection is the process of selecting the most relevant features from a dataset for training the ML model.

Example:

For predicting student marks:

Study Hours       → Useful
Attendance        → Useful
Previous Marks    → Useful
Student ID        → Usually not useful
Favourite Colour  → Usually not useful
Step 5: Train-Test Split
Definition

Train-Test Split is the process of dividing the dataset into training data and testing data.

Common split:

80% → Training
20% → Testing

The exact ratio can vary depending on the problem and dataset.

Step 6: Model Selection
Definition

Model Selection is the process of choosing a suitable Machine Learning algorithm for solving the given problem.

Example:

Classification → Classification Algorithm
Regression     → Regression Algorithm
Clustering     → Clustering Algorithm
Step 7: Model Training
Definition

Model Training is the process of teaching an ML model using training data so that it can learn patterns and relationships.

Training Data
      ↓
ML Algorithm
      ↓
Trained Model
Step 8: Model Testing / Evaluation
Definition

Model Testing is the process of evaluating a trained model using unseen testing data to measure how well it performs.

Step 9: Prediction
Definition

Prediction is the process of using a trained ML model to generate an output for new or unseen data.

Example:

New Student Data
       ↓
Trained Model
       ↓
Predicted Result
